            {"note_id": "FCT_0234", "exact_quote": "When the user enters a floating‑point value like 1.1, use Double.parseDouble (or Float.parseFloat) instead of Integer.parseInt."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0235", "exact_quote": "So, if the user enters 1.1, we cannot use this method, instead we should use float or double, let's say double because that's easier, double parse double, so we parse this number as a double, add 2 to it and then store the result in a double."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0233", "exact_quote": "Parsing a non‑integer string with Integer.parseInt throws an exception."}
