          "evidence": [
            {"note_id": "FCT_0244", "exact_quote": "In java we have this scanner class that is defined in java.util package."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0245", "exact_quote": "Let's import this and create a scanner object, so new scanner."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0246", "exact_quote": "Now here inside this parenthesis, we need to specify where we're going to read data from."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0249", "exact_quote": "To work with the terminal window, we type system.in."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0252", "exact_quote": "So we have system.in, we also have system.out, which we use to print something on the terminal, right?"},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0253", "exact_quote": "Now let's use system.in and terminate this statement with a semicolon."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0254", "exact_quote": "Now this object has a bunch of methods for reading data, and all these methods start with next."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0255", "exact_quote": "There are methods nextByte, nextLine, nextBoolean for reading a byte, a line, and a boolean respectively."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0256", "exact_quote": "Calling the nextByte method returns a byte value that can be stored in a byte variable."}
          ],
